    Allow to escape colons in workflow variable syntax (#6884)
    
    Workflow variables have the following syntax:
    
        ${var:default}
    
    A colon is used to separate the variable name from the default value.
    However, the variable itself might contain a colon and there is
    currently no way to use such a variable. A specific use case is the
    `analyze-mediapackage` operation with `set-tag-variables` enabled. For
    subtitle tracks, this might add a workflow property such as
    
        captions_source_hastag_lang:en
    
    This PR changes the regex to parse variables and allows to escape colons
    in the following way:
    
        ${var-with-\:-colon:default-with\:-colon}
    
    This is breaking in the sense that the string `\:` is now replaced in
    the variable name and default value with a `:`, but I don't think
    anybody used `\:` at the moment. So this should not be breaking in
    practice.
    
    ### How to test this patch
    
    Use a variable with a colon in a workflow.
    
